# KICKBOXING

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

This document defines the physiological, biomechanical, technical and tactical demands of Kickboxing.

Its purpose is to enable the Combat Athlete System (CAS) to understand the unique performance profile of kickboxing athletes and to individualize physical preparation accordingly.

This document describes performance requirements.

It does not prescribe training methods.

---

# Definition

Kickboxing is a striking combat sport combining punches and kicks under a defined ruleset.

Success depends on the athlete's ability to:

Strike efficiently.

Manage distance.

Combine upper and lower body attacks.

Maintain defensive positioning.

Adapt continuously to changing exchanges.

---

# Philosophy

Kickboxing expands the complexity of boxing by introducing lower-limb striking.

The athlete must coordinate punches, kicks, movement and defense while preserving balance and efficiency.

The objective is not to throw more techniques.

The objective is to apply the appropriate technique at the appropriate moment.

