# Final Principle

Kickboxing is not simply boxing with kicks.

It is the integration of upper-body striking,

lower-body striking,

balance,

timing,

movement,

and efficient force transmission.

The athlete who combines these qualities with precision and adaptability creates the greatest probability of success.